In Witch Hat Atelier, [[Magic|magic]] is performed via drawn spells. Each spell has a different effect, decided by the signs and sigils it contains. Spells typically fall into one of five main groups - fire, water, earth, wind, and light - depending on which sigil it possesses.

Unfortunately, the designs of some glyphs have been somewhat inconsistent, so a few spells have different spell construction now than they did earlier on in the story. (This is especially prevalent in the [[Volume 1|first]] and [[Volume 2|second]] volumes). One example of this is how the earth breaker glyphs{{Ref|m|7}} early on in the manga have a levitation keystone in place of an earth sigil. Due to this and similar cases, if a glyph has different forms at different points in the story, the newer version of that glyph will take precedence and become the official form of that glyph.

Each spell has its own page. If you would like to learn more about a specific spell, click on its name to be redirected to that spell's page.

